          "id": "eai-cli-command-contracts",
          "description": "CLI command contracts, including safe immediate child workspace admission errors and synchronous existing-child reuse, local stack compatibility, and deployed read-only CLI smoke. Scoped app sign-in setup verifies the exact complete enrollment and fresh runtime workspace membership, preserves existing credentials without rotation, and retains private local callback settings. Existing PublicAPI enrollment, membership and provisioning wire contracts are unchanged. Exact scoped local setup preserves existing credentials; optional create-local-secret requires enrolled-app/runtime access and exact issuer app/client/tenant proof. Private cooperative lock and pending/issued journal refuse uncertain automatic reissue, recover saved issuance, and require explicit reissue-local-secret consent. Existing deployed command schema and anonymous provisioning denial canaries cover the additive contract. Complete Object Type exports validate every page and compare two scans before atomic output replacement; legacy read DTOs remain lossless. Entra rotation binds the exact app and surfaces safe classified outcomes without repeating mutations. App inventory rejects malformed success payloads. Explicitly unsupported capabilities fail before authentication or network access. Explicit PublicAPI tenant UUIDs use the selected profile and gateway without local tenant-admin discovery or saved selection writes; backend authorization and exact HTTP failure status remain authoritative. Implicit workspace selection retains its existing resolver.",
